The Soldier Who Kept Fighting (Hiroo Onoda) · 3D YouTube Short (1080×1920), style v4 "Toon 3D"

Picture: modelled, lit and animated in code with three.js (MIT). Post (depth of field, bloom, grade): core/three/post.js from
the Lemo-Opuscar library (github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar, MIT). Toon cast with hand-drawn canvas faces (toon.js, with a new
field cap and a patched uniform), and new sets (sets_onoda.js): the jungle of Lubang Island with a hideout and a tally tree, the beach
and a landing boat, a farming village at dusk, a backpacker's camp, a 1974 used-book shop, a four-engine plane and an airliner.
The people are stylised stand-ins with no real likeness; the leaflet, newspaper and order texts are illustrations (see FACTS.md).

Style: techniques studied from a reference Short supplied by the creator (see style/REFERENCE.md); characters, designs,
story and assets here are original.

Voice-over: ElevenLabs v4 (voice preset "Harrison", the same voice as The Pudding Guy) through the creator's Higgsfield account,
one read of all nine lines; pauses tightened and sped up 22 % (pitch unchanged) in timing.py. Check Higgsfield's / ElevenLabs' terms
for your use.

Fonts: Montserrat (SIL OFL 1.1, fonts/OFL-Montserrat.txt); Fredoka (SIL OFL 1.1, fonts/OFL-Fredoka.txt).
Music and sound effects: synthesised in code (music.py; synth_lib.py from the Lemo-Opuscar library, MIT). No samples.
